dated market terms prevent a forward-access conclusion. The alleged maturity conflict is withdrawn; full instrument/amortization allocation and operative call terms remain distinct limitations."},{"old":"Missing: policy commitments, reconciled instrument maturities, accepted earnings, forecasts and legal/market inputs. No maturity bucket is repaired by assumption.","new":"Missing: policy commitments, full instrument/amortization allocation, operative call terms, accepted earnings, forecasts and legal/market inputs. Reported maturity dates are supplied; no maturity bucket is repaired by assumption."},{"old":"Resolve maturity conflict before calendar-based conclusions.","new":"Use corrected reported dates and unchanged fiscal buckets; the calendar-fiscal conflict finding is withdrawn, not an issuer inconsistency."},{"old":"Basis: X06/BF02/C02; route to CP-3C.","new":"Basis: X06/BF02 and corrected C02; route to CP-3C. C02 records a withdrawn host/model error, not adverse issuer evidence."},{"old":"| Revolver | September 30, 2024 commitments USD 910 million; reported available USD 843 million; February 2029 maturity | CP-1 F06; no drawn balance inferred and no addition to cash as certified usable liquidity |","new":"| Revolver | September 30, 2024 commitments USD 910 million; reported available USD 843 million; outstanding letters of credit USD 67 million; February 27, 2029 maturity | CP-1 F06; directly confirmed S1 p.45. USD 67 million is the sourced LC amount, not inferred drawn borrowing; no addition to cash as certified usable liquidity |"},{"old":"| Maturity-allocation conflict | Due-2027 notes principal USD 2,650 million versus reported fiscal-2027 schedule USD 92 million | CP-1 D03/MAT03 and CP-1A C02; preserve both; no reconciled maturity wall or reassignment |","new":"| Corrected calendar/fiscal mapping — conflict withdrawn | 5.50% notes principal USD 2,650 million due November 15, 2027, in fiscal 2028; reported fiscal-2027 schedule USD 92 million unchanged | CP-1 D03/MAT03 and corrected CP-1A C02; S1 p.43 explicitly states no tranche of term loans or notes matures until November 2027 (fiscal 2028), and p.46 supplies the exact date. The earlier conflict was a host/model calendar-fiscal error, not an issuer inconsistency; no reassignment or issuer reconciliation solely for that error |"},{"old":"No sum of cash and facilities, post-event cash rollforward, sustainable FCF, forecast, pro forma acquired earnings, price/volume bridge, quantitative stress or legal-capacity calculation is created.","new":"Reported long-term debt repayment buckets excluding finance leases remain FY2025 USD 93 million, FY2026 USD 92 million, FY2027 USD 92 million, FY2028 USD 6,637 million, FY2029 USD 4,768 million and thereafter USD 12,637 million (CP-1 MAT01–MAT06; S1 p.133). Short-term A/R securitization remains separate. Correct date mapping does not establish a full instrument/amortization allocation.

S1 p.46 supplies exact annual-reported note maturities: 5.50% 2027 notes November 15, 2027; 6.75% 2028 notes August 15, 2028; 4.625% 2029 notes January 15, 2029; 6.375% 2029 notes March 1, 2029; 4.875% 2029 notes May 1, 2029; 6.875% 2030 notes December 15, 2030; 7.125% 2031 notes December 1, 2031; 6.625% 2032 notes March 1, 2032; 6.00% 2033 notes January 15, 2033. Amounts/rates are unchanged; call schedules are not inferred. Annual-reported January 15, 2033 does not fill the supplied legal note form's blank day or substitute for an authenticated issued note, which is Not supplied; coupon/call dates do not fill that form.

No sum of cash and facilities, post-event cash rollforward, sustainable FCF, forecast, pro forma acquired earnings, price/volume bridge, quantitative stress or legal-capacity calculation is created."},{"old":"| Maturity allocation — CP-1 G13; CP-1A C02/G04 | Material | Due-2027 instrument and fiscal-year schedule conflict; older call/exact maturity terms and live status remain unresolved. | Date-specific refinancing burden | CP-3C obtains issuer reconciliation and controlling instrument terms. Preserve observations rather than repair the wall. |","new":"| Operative refinancing terms — corrected CP-1 G13; CP-1A C02/G04 | Material for operative/forward conclusions | Exact annual-reported note dates and revolver maturity are supplied. Full instrument/amortization allocation, operative call terms, authenticated issued 2033 note and live status remain separate limitations; the calendar-fiscal conflict is withdrawn. | Operative terms and forward refinancing capacity, not an unresolved FY2027 maturity gap | CP-3C obtains controlling terms and dated live evidence as required. Retain all fiscal buckets including FY2027 92; no issuer reconciliation request solely for the withdrawn host/model error. |"},{"old":"Identify additional controlling facilities, ICA/security, certificates and usage evidence before whole-package or numerical capacity conclusions. No legal permission or compliance opinion is inherited from CP-2.","new":"S1 pp.44–45 supplies summarized combined TD Group, TransDigm Inc. and other guarantor financial data, excluding non-issuers/non-guarantors and eliminating intercompany balances/transactions among included entities; dealings/balances with excluded entities are separately presented. This is not an individual entity/collateral/perfection/value map or allowed-claims waterfall. Identify additional controlling facilities, ICA/security, certificates and usage evidence before whole-package or numerical capacity conclusions. No legal permission or compliance opinion is inherited from CP-2."},{"old":"Retain Medium confidence and absent market/portfolio/forecast/legal inputs; no security recommendation, sizing or clearance follows.","new":"Retain Medium confidence and absent market/portfolio/forecast/legal inputs; no security recommendation, sizing or clearance follows. Review corrected CP-5 when available (no CP-5 handoff is supplied here): its three prior instruction-context false positives stay withdrawn, and its maturity-conflict finding must be withdrawn as a host/model calendar-fiscal error with S1 pp.43/46 proof, not evidence against the issuer or an unresolved maturity gap. The lease narrative, cash-bridge and dividend-scope issues remain for independent assessment."},{"old":"Historical extensions, secured substitution, maturity conflict and cash-retention sensitivity","new":"Historical extensions, secured substitution, corrected reported maturity dates and cash-retention sensitivity"},{"old":"Reconcile instrument maturities and obtain dated terms/market access before forward execution conclusions. No coercive LME or refinancing failure is established.","new":"Use supplied reported maturity dates and unchanged fiscal buckets; obtain full instrument/amortization mapping, operative terms and dated market-access evidence before forward execution conclusions. No reconciliation request solely for the withdrawn calendar-fiscal error. No coercive LME or refinancing failure is established."}] }
